common-passwords.txt.gz
-----------------------
Contents: the 20 000 most frequent entries (one password per line, in
          frequency order) of zxcvbn's data/passwords.txt.
Source:   Dropbox zxcvbn, https://github.com/dropbox/zxcvbn
Version:  commit 67c4ece9efc40c9d0a1d7d995b2b22a91be500c2
          (data/passwords.txt, SHA-256
          6313cc5ef683a0461416318ee3b16f3d771a3cd10ea2aae54571d27ff95d951f)
Licence:  MIT (the zxcvbn repository's LICENSE.txt), reproduced below.
Built by: scripts/build_common_passwords.py (pinned commit and checksum;
          `--check` verifies this file against a fresh build).

Provenance note: zxcvbn's README credits "Mark Burnett for releasing his
10M password corpus", which was reported in 2015 as released to the public
domain; the zxcvbn repository states no separate licence for its data files,
which are distributed under the repository's MIT licence. The list contains
passwords only (no usernames or other personal data).

